From: guillermo <guillermo.karsz@solid-run.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bootmenu: start SWUpdate when the SCU remote-update flag is set

Hailo's run_swupdate.sh (single mode) writes the SCU bootloader
configuration with boot_image_mode = 1 ("remote update") and reboots.
U-Boot's board code exports that field as ${boot_image_mode}; Hailo's
own boot menus (since v1.9.0) test it and run boot_swupdate_mmc, which
loads the SWUpdate ramdisk from the eMMC boot partition.

The SolidRun board header replaces Hailo's environment and its default
menu entry booted straight from eMMC, so the flag was ignored and the
Linux-initiated update never started (the board simply rebooted into
the old system with the flag left set in qSPI).

Add the same test in front of the default "Boot from eMMC" entry. The
SWUpdate ramdisk clears the flag when the update finishes, so the
following boots are normal again. The U-Boot menu entry "SWUpdate"
keeps working unchanged.

Signed-off-by: guillermo <guillermo.karsz@solid-run.com>
---
 include/configs/hailo15-solidrun.h | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/configs/hailo15-solidrun.h b/include/configs/hailo15-solidrun.h
--- a/include/configs/hailo15-solidrun.h
+++ b/include/configs/hailo15-solidrun.h
@@ -19,7 +19,11 @@
 
 #define BOOTMENU \
     /* Try all boot options by order */ \
-    "bootmenu_0=Boot from eMMC=run boot_mmc1\0" \
+    /* boot_image_mode = 1 means Linux requested a remote update */ \
+    /* (/etc/run_swupdate.sh): start SWUpdate like Hailo's boards do */ \
+    "bootmenu_0=Boot from eMMC=" \
+        "if test ${boot_image_mode} = 1; then run boot_swupdate_mmc; exit 1; fi; " \
+        "run boot_mmc1\0" \
     "bootmenu_1=Boot to flashing ramdisk=run boot_flashing_ramdisk\0" \
     "bootmenu_2=SWUpdate=run boot_swupdate_mmc\0" \
     "default_spl_boot_source=mmc2\0" \
